  "final_message": "I have started listing the repository files and will inspect the codebase once complete.\nI am waiting for the file listing to finish.\nI have executed `git grep \"channel\"` to find all usages across the codebase and am waiting for the results.\nI have executed `npm test` to verify current test status and am waiting for the test suite to finish.\nI have run `npm run arch` to verify dependency-cruiser rules and am waiting for the check to complete.\nI have run `git log` to inspect commit history and am waiting for the command to finish.\nI have run a search for deprecation references across the repository and am waiting for the results.\nI have searched for ARCH references across the codebase and am waiting for the command to finish.\nI cannot drop `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates architectural rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be dropped directly\n\n1. **Cross-repository contract**: Even though internal code in this service does not read `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26), the event is published via Kafka to external services in separate repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing the field is a breaking change for those consumers.\n2. **Additive-only policy**: Under ARCH-4, schema changes must be strictly additive. Removals and renames must follow a coordinated deprecation process across all consuming services rather than an immediate deletion.\n3. **API & Model dependency**: Dropping `channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38) would break [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) event creation and introduce breaking changes to clients sending `POST /orders`.\n\n### Recommended Path\n\nIf `channel` is to be phased out:\n1. Coordinate with the downstream teams (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) to ensure their consumers have stopped relying on the field.\n2. Mark the field as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) during the transition window.\n3. Remove the field only after the deprecation period and schema version rollout are complete.\n",
